abstract = {This paper conducts an in-depth study on the safety of civil engineering structures, and uses neural network algorithms in computer algorithms to construct a structural safety assessment model based on the collection of bridge stress, strain, displacement and other data. In the research process, the system architecture and model construction, model training and optimization, application, etc. are carried out. Experiments have shown that the system can accurately predict the health of the structure, and the health score can be reduced from 90 to 75 under wind load conditions, but can be increased to 85 points based on timely maintenance. This shows that the application of computer algorithms in the safety assessment of civil engineering structures is of great significance, which can effectively improve the accuracy and timeliness of monitoring and evaluation.},
