abstract = {In the intelligent era, combinatorial optimization problems—such as those in logistics scheduling, resource allocation, and intelligent transportation—have become increasingly prominent as core issues in numerous fields. Meanwhile, the rapid development of intelligent technologies has brought new opportunities for solving combinatorial optimization problems. This paper first introduces the basic concepts and classifications of combinatorial optimization problems. It then uses the bibliometric tool Citespace to analyze literature on digital-intelligent combinatorial optimization. Additionally, it comprehensively reviews and analyzes recent research progress from two core dimensions: intelligent optimization algorithms and artificial intelligence algorithms. The paper also summarizes application cases of combinatorial optimization methods in the intelligent era, such as logistics supply chain optimization, transportation route planning, manufacturing optimization, and financial prediction optimization, and discusses the shortcomings of current research. Finally, it prospects future research directions, providing important references for the theoretical development of combinatorial optimization.},
